schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "\"The Web3 community is remarkably generous with time and knowledge\""
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    "The Web3 community is remarkably generous with time and knowledge."
    Framed as the closing encouragement to reach out and ask for help.
  evidence: >-
    No citation, study, or specific example is given in the article; it is
    presented as the author's own observation/encouragement.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/finding-support-mentorship.md (no external source cited)
  interpretation: >-
    A motivational generalization rather than a verifiable claim; plausible
    given the mentorship/peer-support culture described elsewhere on the site
    (e.g. Greenpill's tiered participation model), but not independently
    evidenced here.
  uncertainty: >-
    Anecdotal / unsourced. Should not be read as a measured or universal
    claim about the whole web3 community, which the site elsewhere
    acknowledges includes scams and bad actors alongside generous ones.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
